# Blaze of Glory: "Cast this spell only during combat before blockers are declared" (CR 601.3) and "Target creature defending
# player controls can block any number of creatures this turn. It blocks each attacking creature this turn if able." Bot1
# attacks with three 2/2s; before combat the spell is refused (the positive control is the cast in the declare attackers
# step). Bot2's Ironroot Treefolk (3/5) then blocks all three: a declaration leaving one out is refused (CR 509.1c, the
# requirement is obeyed as far as it can be), as is blocking just one. Its 3 damage is divided among the three it blocks
# (CR 510.1d): 2 kills the Bears, 1 goes to Bear Cub, none to the Apes. The Treefolk takes 6 and dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Balduvian Bears
Bear Cub
Barbary Apes
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Ironroot Treefolk
Mox Pearl
Blaze of Glory
Island x14

